consisting of vancomycin, eremomycin, chloroeremomycin, and β-avoparcin, more preferably A2-A -A-rA5-A6-A7 is as found in vancomycin. In other preferred compounds of the present invention, the Cδ position of the glucose residue attached to A4 is modified to bear at least one substituent other than hydroxyl, and more preferably the at least one substituent other than hydroxyl is a polar substituent or a hydrophobic substituent. In preferred compounds of the present invention where A2-A -A4-A5-A-6-A7 is as found in vancomycin, the vancosamine residue in vancomycin is N-substituted with said at least one hydrophobic substituent. In other preferred compounds of the present invention wherein A2-A3-A -A5-A6-A7 is as found in vancomycin, the glucose residue attached to i of vancomycin is modified at the C6 position to bear at least one substituent other than hydroxyl, preferably a polar substituent, and said vancosamine residue is N-substituted with said at least one hydrophobic substituent. The at least one hydrophobic substituent is preferably selected from R, OR, NR,R, SR, SO2R, C(O)OR, C(O)SR, C(S)OR, C(S)SR, NRιC(O)R, C(O)NR,R, or halo and R is alkyl, aryl, aralk"\ alkanoyl, aroyl, aralkanoyl, heterocyclic, heterocyclic-carbonyl, heterocyclic-alkyl, heterocyclic-alkyl-carbonyl, alkylsulfonyl or arylsulfonyl; 

 is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, aralkyl, alkanoyl, aroyl, aralkanoyl, heterocyclic, heterocyclic-carbonyl, heterocyclic-alkyl, heterocyclic-alkyl-carbonyl, alkylsulfonyl or arylsulfonyl; and any pharmaceutically acceptable salts thereof; and if two or more of said substituents are present, they can be the same or different. The organic group A. in the preferred compounds of the present invention, is preferably an organic group selected from the group consisting of a modified or unmodified alpha amino acid residue other than N-substituted 

leucine, alkyl, aryl, aralkyl, alkanoyl, aroyl, aralkanoyl, heterocyclic, heterocyclic-carbonyl, heterocyclic-alkyl, heterocyclic-alkyl-carbonyl, alkylsulfonyl, arylsulfonyl, guanidinyl, carbamoyl, or xanthyl. Also, in the preferred compounds of the present invention, the A7 group bears a terminal carboxyl, ester, thioester, amide, N-substituted amide, or other carboxylic acid derivative, any of which groups may be substituted with any of the substituents described herein.
